**Playwright through the @playwright/test runner, run by `bun run e2e`** (#werk-test-runner). Not an MCP server, not the client runner's browser mode.

A visual test boots werk the way a person does — a real werk server on a copy of the fixture log, the real routes, the real SSE stream — then opens Chromium, navigates, clicks, asserts, and writes a PNG to a directory. A fake `claude` is first on PATH, so no spec reaches a real agent.

This is the only option that covers the whole running loop. The other two mount a component or steer a browser from outside, and neither holds the server's claude child through a turn.

The cost is a heavy dependency: a browser binary.

What a run asserts, and what happens to the PNG, is #werk-test-visual-judge.

